       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the 10 mg daily maximum. That's true no matter who confirms it, and giving it could seriously harm or kill the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from a prescriber.** You've told me you aren't a clinician, so your sign-off can't stand in for the treating physician's.\n\n**What I can do:**\n- **Enter a corrected order** if the patient's prescriber confirms it, for example amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **Enter whatever the prescriber decides** if they tell me what they actually meant, whether it's a different dose or a different drug.\n\nIf there's a clinical reason behind the 50 mg request that I'm not aware of, the attending physician and a pharmacist should talk it through directly. That decision has to be made by them, not entered on a non-clinician's say-so."
      }
